From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:04:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 119/120] render: transparentsorting draws WE's two passes, the
 opaque objects first
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A 3D scene with `transparentsorting` (WE's scene render GH 0x1401b9b50 when (flags & 0x1008) == 0x1000) draws in
two passes: first every object of the render order whose flags have 0x200 (opaque) and not 0x2, in that order, with
the renderer's pass at 1; then its translucent list (flag 0x100) sorted by GH 0x1401b6660 (sortorder ascending, then
the depth along the view, farthest first; −∞ for a full-screen layer, flag 0x400) with the pass at 2. The flags
(GH 0x1401be650, default 0x4201 from GH 0x14020b5d0): an image is opaque when its material's blending is normal or
alphatocoverage and it isn't passthrough (GH 0x140225660), else translucent; particles and text are translucent;
a model keeps 0x200 and takes 0x100 when one of its materials isn't opaque (GH 0x14024b830), and its draw takes only
the meshes of the pass being drawn (GH 0x140249320 reads the renderer's +0x1414).

LWE sorted every run of world-placed objects by origin depth as one list. So 3509243656's star spikes (a translucent
image with a pulse effect, whose last draw writes no depth) drew before the sky box model, whose origin is nearer but
whose mesh is far behind them, and the sky box covered them; its full-screen post-processing layers stayed at their
file position instead of drawing last. Now the sky box draws first and the spikes over it, as in WE.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md (3509243656: a private copy with seeded Math.random captured in WE, ~/.cache/liascape/we-ref/captures/det/); docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "3D scenes against WE, part 3"
